<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon's foreground layer: a shell prompt, `>` and a cursor rule.

  WHY THIS MARK. The product is a terminal multi-agent tracker, and the prompt chevron is the
  one symbol that reads as "terminal" at 48dp without any detail to lose. It carries no text,
  so it needs no localisation and no font, and it is a single stroke weight, so it survives
  the monochrome and themed-icon treatments Android applies without becoming a smudge.

  WHY IT IS A VECTOR AND WHY THERE ARE NO PNG BUCKETS. minSdk is 33 and adaptive icons landed
  at 26, so mipmap-anydpi-v26 resolves on every device this app supports; a density ladder of
  rasterised copies would be twelve files that can disagree with each other and with this one.

  GEOMETRY. The canvas is the adaptive 108x108dp. Everything here sits inside the 66dp safe
  circle the launcher mask is guaranteed not to clip: the drawn extent including stroke width
  spans roughly x 34.5..75.5 and y 38.5..69.5, whose furthest corner is about 26.5dp from the
  centre against the 33dp the safe circle allows. A mark that merely looks centred is one that
  a round mask on someone else's launcher crops.

  COLOUR IS A TOKEN, NOT A VALUE. swarm_text_primary is the same origin every other colour in
  this app comes from (android/design-tokens.tsv, PB-TOK-1). An icon-only literal would be a
  colour that entered the product without passing through that origin, which is precisely what
  the token gate exists to refuse.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The chevron. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M38,42 L52,54 L38,66"
        android:strokeColor="@color/swarm_text_primary"
        android:strokeWidth="7"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round" />

    <!-- The cursor rule, on the prompt's baseline. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M59,66 L72,66"
        android:strokeColor="@color/swarm_text_primary"
        android:strokeWidth="7"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />
</vector>
